@startuml CrossView Consistency Considerations

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam noteBorderColor gray
skinparam noteBackgroundColor lightyellow

' Define the architectural views as components
component "Operational View" as OV #Gold
component "Functional View" as FV #LightGreen
component "Deployment View" as DV #LightBlue
component "Information View" as IV #LightPink
component "Development View" as DevV #LightGray
component "Concurrency View" as CV #LightCyan

' Set direction for better layout
left to right direction

' Define relationships between views
OV -- FV : "must align with"
note on link
    Operational monitoring capabilities must align with functional elements
    - Each functional component must have corresponding operational support
    - Changes to functional components require updates to monitoring configurations
end note

OV -- DV : "must integrate with"
note on link
    Installation model must be consistent with physical deployment topology
    - Cloud deployment architecture must match server configurations
    - Operational monitoring must account for all deployed components
end note

OV -- IV : "must ensure consistency for"
note on link
    Backup and restore strategies must account for all data entities
    - Data protection mechanisms must preserve relationships defined in Information View
    - Recovery operations must maintain data integrity and consistency
end note

OV -- DevV : "must coordinate with"
note on link
    Operational tools must follow module organization standards
    - Monitoring interfaces must adhere to coding standards
    - Support systems must integrate with development frameworks
end note

OV -- CV : "must monitor"
note on link
    Operational monitoring of real-time features must align with concurrency models
    - Performance metrics must account for simultaneous user interactions
    ' - Resource allocation must support game state management requirements
end note

' Maintaining consistency section
note bottom of OV
    <b>Maintaining Consistency</b>
    - New functions need monitoring updates.
    - Deployment changes require installation updates.
    - Data model changes need backup adjustments.
    - Development updates affect monitoring.
    - Concurrency must align with monitoring.
   
end note

 ' - Regular cross-view reviews during architectural updates
    ' - Explicit traceability between related elements
    ' - Collaborative design sessions across operational domains
    ' - Validation through integrated testing

@enduml